  "hints": [
    "Two strings are rearrangements of each other exactly when their letter counts match. Every candidate window has the same length.",
    "Slide a fixed-size window: when it moves right by one, one letter enters and one leaves, so update the counts instead of recounting.",
    "Keep 26 counts of code minus window, plus a counter of how many letters are nonzero. Adjust both on each enter/leave and record the start when the counter is 0."
  ],
  "solution": {
    "js": "function scrambledStarts(text, code) {\n  const m = code.length\n  const out = []\n  if (m > text.length) return out\n  const diff = new Array(26).fill(0)\n  const idx = ch => ch.charCodeAt(0) - 97\n  for (const ch of code) diff[idx(ch)]++\n  let off = diff.filter(x => x !== 0).length\n  const bump = (ch, d) => {\n    const k = idx(ch)\n    if (diff[k] === 0) off++\n    diff[k] += d\n    if (diff[k] === 0) off--\n  }\n  for (let r = 0; r < text.length; r++) {\n    bump(text[r], -1)\n    if (r >= m) bump(text[r - m], 1)\n    if (r >= m - 1 && off === 0) out.push(r - m + 1)\n  }\n  return out\n}\n",
    "py": "def scrambled_starts(text, code):\n    m = len(code)\n    out = []\n    if m > len(text):\n        return out\n    diff = [0] * 26\n    for ch in code:\n        diff[ord(ch) - 97] += 1\n    off = sum(1 for x in diff if x)\n\n    def bump(ch, d):\n        nonlocal off\n        k = ord(ch) - 97\n        if diff[k] == 0:\n            off += 1\n        diff[k] += d\n        if diff[k] == 0:\n            off -= 1\n\n    for r, ch in enumerate(text):\n        bump(ch, -1)\n        if r >= m:\n            bump(text[r - m], 1)\n        if r >= m - 1 and off == 0:\n            out.append(r - m + 1)\n    return out\n",
    "explanation": "diff holds code's letter counts minus the window's, and off counts letters whose difference is nonzero, so a match is exactly off == 0. Each slide changes two counts in O(1), so we never recount a window."
  },
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n + m)",
    "space": "O(1)",
    "notes": "The count array has a fixed 26 entries. Comparing two 26-entry arrays each step would also be linear, with a larger constant."
  },
  "followUps": [
    "Return only whether at least one such window exists, stopping early.",
    "How would you handle a full Unicode alphabet efficiently?"
  ]
}
